# React Frontend Conventions

## Stack
React 18 + TypeScript (strict) + Vite + TanStack Query + shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS.
Do not install Angular, Vue, or any conflicting UI framework.

## Component structure
```
src/
  components/    Shared UI components (shadcn wrappers, design system)
  features/      Feature folders (dashboard/, risk/, interventions/, reports/)
  hooks/         Custom React hooks (useTenantContext, useRiskProfile, etc.)
  lib/           API clients, utilities, Protobuf decoders
  pages/         Route-level page components
```

## Data fetching
Use TanStack Query (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) for all server state. Never use `useEffect` + `fetch` manually.

```tsx
// BAD
useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/employees').then(...) }, []);

// GOOD
const { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['employees', tenantId], queryFn: fetchEmployees });
```

## Charting
Use **ApexCharts** (`react-apexcharts`) as the default. Use D3.js only for custom non-standard visualisations. Do not add Chart.js.

Every chart must have an accessible alternative — either a visible data table or `aria-label` with a summary.

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA — non-negotiable)
- Never suppress focus indicators with `outline: none` or `outline: 0` without a visible replacement.
- Risk badges must use colour + icon + text — never colour alone.
- All form errors must be associated with the input via `aria-describedby`.
- All interactive elements must be keyboard operable (Tab / Enter / Space / Arrow keys).
- Minimum contrast ratio: 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text.

## Tenant context
Read `tenantId` and user roles from a `useTenantContext()` hook that parses the JWT claims stored in session. Never hard-code tenant IDs.

## WebSocket (live alerts)
Use the `useAtRiskAlerts()` hook that connects via STOMP over WebSocket for live dashboard updates. Fall back to SSE if WebSocket is unavailable.
